 "request": {
  "model": "deepseek-flash",
  "messages": [
   {
    "role": "system",
    "content": "You build one part in a CAD kernel by calling tools. Each tool is one operation; the kernel's inspection after it comes back to you.\nLengths are {\"value\": <number>, \"unit\": \"mm\" | \"cm\" | \"m\" | \"in\"}. Sketches lie on a plane through the origin: \"top\" is XY, \"front\" is XZ, \"right\" is YZ.\nextrude and cut take a sketch id. Holes are drilled along Z from the top of the part at XY positions. Fillet and chamfer edges are named \"<feature id>:edge:<n>\":\ncall inspect first, which lists the solid's edges with their name, type, centre and direction, and take the names from that list.\nA hexagon's across-flats size is the distance between two opposite sides; its corners lie across_flats / √3 from its centre.\nA document starts with new_part. Give every operation a new id. If an operation is refused or fails, read its error and correct it.\nWhen the request is done, reply with one line and call no tool."
   },
   {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "The document does not exist yet.\nBuild this part: A 40 mm x 40 mm x 5 mm plate with a 6 mm through hole centred 30 mm from the plate centre along X.\nSpec, lengths also in mm: {\"part\":\"rectangular plate with through hole\",\"dimensions\":[{\"name\":\"plate length along X\",\"value\":40,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"mm\":40},{\"name\":\"plate width along Y\",\"value\":40,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"mm\":40},{\"name\":\"plate thickness\",\"value\":5,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"mm\":5},{\"name\":\"hole diameter\",\"value\":6,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"mm\":6},{\"name\":\"hole centre offset from plate centre along X\",\"value\":30,\"unit\":\"mm\",\"mm\":30}],\"envelope_mm\":[40,40,5],\"assumptions\":[\"hole goes through\",\"edges sharp\",\"hole offset along +X\"]}"
   },
   {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "I'll start by creating the part and inspecting the initial state.",
